<title>MEXICO: Mexico Jan silver output up, other metals detailed.</title>
<headline>Mexico Jan silver output up, other metals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest silver producer, saw output rise in January to 239,954 kilograms from 218,958 kgs in the same month in 1996, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said Monday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of metals and minerals production for the first month of 1997 were as follows:  </p>
<p>    Product	Jan 97	 Jan 96    Pct Chge vs 95</p>
<p>    Gold	    2,198	  1,910	   15.1</p>
<p>    Silver	239,954	218,958	    9.6</p>
<p>    Lead	   19,244	 12,993	   48.1</p>
<p>    Copper	 21,903	 29,052	  -24.6</p>
<p>    Zinc	   31,457	 29,878	    5.3</p>
<p>    Coal	  764,280	620,257	   23.2</p>
<p>    Iron	  456,407	470,341	   -3.0</p>
<p>    Sulphur	75,322	 81,274	   -7.3</p>
<p>    Dolomite     60,854	 80,273	    N/A</p>
<p>    Gypsum	369,040	261,358	   41.2</p>
<p>    Phosphorite  53,266	 51,757	    N/A</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals output in kgs, others in tonnes. Coal output in mineral volume.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9530)).</p>
</text>
